    <technology>
      <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>The mining activity consists of two main phases: the extraction of sand and gravel from natural deposits and subsequent processing.  &#13;
The processing usually consists of a screening line to produce the various sand and round gravel granulometry and a parallel line for shredding and screening the coarser fractions to make the "split". In addition, the sands are usually subjected to washing and cyclone cycles to separate the ultra-fine and silty substances that take root on their surface and must be removed when you want to use the sands in cement and bitumen production. &#13;
 &#13;
Good the Reliability;   &#13;
Very Good the Geographical representativeness;   &#13;
Very Good the Time representativeness;   &#13;
Very Good the Technological representativeness. </technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
      <technologicalApplicability>Extraction of a tonne of the natural mixture from a sand and gravel quarry located in the Lombardy Region. </technologicalApplicability>
    </technology>
  </processInformation>
